---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { DATES, fmt } from '@/lib/timeline';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About the OZ 2.0 State-Specific Resource.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">About</h1>

    <p class="text-oz-neutral-700 mb-4">
      The 2025 One Big Beautiful Bill Act made Opportunity Zones permanent and reset the map.
      There is good national-level coverage from EIG, Novogradac, and the OZ industry press.
      There is almost no resource that helps a planner in a rural-eligible county figure out
      which tracts they have, who to convene, and how OZ stacks with other federal capital.
    </p>
    <p class="text-oz-neutral-700 mb-4">
      This is that resource. It is neutral, evidence-based, and designed to be useful
      regardless of political stance. It does not advocate for or against designation —
      it helps planners understand their options and engage the process.
    </p>
    <p class="text-oz-neutral-700 mb-4">
      Phase 1 covered the nomination round: all 50 states and DC were live by mid-June 2026,
      before the federal window opened {fmt(DATES.windowOpens)}. With that window closed and
      designations taking effect {fmt(DATES.designationsEffective)}, the work shifts from helping
      communities get tracts nominated to helping them understand what was designated, what the
      capital actually does once it arrives, and whether OZ 2.0 performs any better than OZ 1.0 did.
      The new § 6039K reporting regime will, for the first time, make that last question
      answerable — see <a href="/whats-next#reporting" class="text-oz-blue underline">what happens next</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-oz-neutral-700 mb-8">
      Maintained by <a href="https://vargo.city" class="text-oz-blue underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jason Vargo</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Scope</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-oz-neutral-500 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mb-8">
      <li>50 states + DC spotlight pages</li>
      <li>Coalition playbook, capital stack guide, OZ 1.0 evidence summary</li>
      <li>OZ 1.0 case study library and the finance study guide</li>
      <li>Program timeline, Notice 2026-40 transition rules, and the OZ reporting rule</li>
      <li>Off-list nomination (Section 5.04) explainer</li>
      <li>Native/tribal callout on every applicable state page</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Not in scope</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-oz-neutral-500 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Eligibility maps (embedded from EIG and IRS)</li>
      <li>Investor fund discovery</li>
      <li>The 5 U.S. territories (Phase 2)</li>
      <li>Editorial framing on displacement or gentrification (separate essay)</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
